00:37:09,443 --> 00:37:13,031
- You can't tell the
difference with their hats off.

1062
00:37:13,031 --> 00:37:14,239
- It looks like you had this room done

1063
00:37:14,239 --> 00:37:15,993
in early paleolithic here.

1064
00:37:15,993 --> 00:37:19,069
(chuckling)

1065
00:37:19,069 --> 00:37:22,152
- Hey, this music wasn't here before.

1066
00:37:23,564 --> 00:37:25,731
- Elk Master on the scene.

1067
00:37:30,118 --> 00:37:32,200
- Someplace, make a nice Elks hall,

1068
00:37:32,200 --> 00:37:33,033
you know that?

1069
00:37:33,033 --> 00:37:35,834
- Where would the Brewmeister
and the pull tabs go?

1070
00:37:35,834 --> 00:37:38,009
- You think we'll find that
girl's pa in here alive?

1071
00:37:38,009 --> 00:37:38,842
- Hell no.

1072
00:37:38,842 --> 00:37:40,183
Oh sorry.

1073
00:37:40,183 --> 00:37:42,929
- The spiders have a habit of
stunning their prey with venom

1074
00:37:42,929 --> 00:37:43,918
and storing them in a silk bag

1075
00:37:43,918 --> 00:37:45,712
til they're ready to feed on them.

1076
00:37:45,712 --> 00:37:46,828
- Like an Anne Klein?

1077
00:37:46,828 --> 00:37:48,003
- I suppose.

1078
00:37:48,003 --> 00:37:49,484
- Not quite.

1079
00:37:49,484 --> 00:37:50,600
They drain the liquid from the bodies,

1080
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,243
leaving only the skin and bones.

1081
00:37:52,243 --> 00:37:53,944
- So we're looking for a drunk spider?

1082
00:37:53,944 --> 00:37:55,252
- Mind you've got.

1083
00:37:55,252 --> 00:37:57,594
Alright, let's look for Flynn,

1084
00:37:57,594 --> 00:37:59,263
and don't lose sight
of the man next to you.

1085
00:37:59,263 --> 00:38:01,195
No sense in anyone getting lost.

1086
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:03,056
- Well, look for a dry guy in a silk bag.

1087
00:38:03,056 --> 00:38:04,139
Pass it down.

1088
00:38:07,405 --> 00:38:08,990
- Buddy up and enjoy the scenery.

1089
00:38:08,990 --> 00:38:11,073
No sense in wasting that.

1090
00:38:12,822 --> 00:38:13,935
- Oh wait a minute.

1091
00:38:13,935 --> 00:38:15,867
That says Arne Saknussemm on this wall.

1092
00:38:15,867 --> 00:38:17,235
- This is a waste of time.

1093
00:38:17,235 --> 00:38:18,685
You know something?

1094
00:38:18,685 --> 00:38:19,993
I haven't seen a spider yet,

1095
00:38:19,993 --> 00:38:22,101
and I don't think we will.

1096
00:38:22,101 --> 00:38:23,849
- You will if he's still there.

1097
00:38:23,849 --> 00:38:26,873
- It'd be just dialogue if he
moved into the next county.

1098
00:38:26,873 --> 00:38:27,827
(laughing)

1099
00:38:27,827 --> 00:38:29,802
- I don't think you'll be disappointed.

1100
00:38:29,802 --> 00:38:31,598
There's something in here all right.

1101
00:38:31,598 --> 00:38:33,187
You'd naturally expect
to find a certain amount

1102
00:38:33,187 --> 00:38:34,843
of wildlife in a cave.

1103
00:38:34,843 --> 00:38:36,199
Rats, mice, bats, and so on.

1104
00:38:36,199 --> 00:38:37,567
- The occasional Japanese soldier.

1105
00:38:37,567 --> 00:38:38,567
- You don't.

1106
00:38:39,857 --> 00:38:42,421
They've been frightened out.

1107
00:38:42,421 --> 00:38:43,254
- Ah.

1108
00:38:45,379 --> 00:38:46,462
- I'm Batman.

1109
00:38:48,639 --> 00:38:50,194
(rifle shooting)

1110
00:38:50,194 --> 00:38:53,527
- Oh, now we have to pay Jack Nicholson.

1111
00:38:55,130 --> 00:38:56,857
- No wildlife, eh Kingman?

1112
00:38:56,857 --> 00:38:58,024
- Not anymore.

1113
00:38:59,341 --> 00:39:02,239
- That's about as big
as they come, I'd say.

1114
00:39:02,239 --> 00:39:04,708
- I wouldn't handle it if I
were you. It might have rabies.

1115
00:39:04,708 --> 00:39:06,041
- Or girl germs.

1116
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:09,820
(eerie music)

1117
00:39:15,165 --> 00:39:19,165
- I know that theremin
is around here somewhere.

1118
00:39:27,860 --> 00:39:28,693
- Are you happy now?

1119
00:39:28,693 --> 00:39:29,693
I buried it.

1120
00:39:31,092 --> 00:39:33,150
- There, it's buried.

1121
00:39:33,150 --> 00:39:35,471
Want to say a few words over it, Sheriff?

1122
00:39:35,471 --> 00:39:36,304
- Oh sure.

1123
00:39:36,304 --> 00:39:39,971
Dear Lord-
(Carol screaming)

1124
00:39:40,826 --> 00:39:42,625
(crying)

1125
00:39:42,625 --> 00:39:45,443
- Oh, the snap's in the front, you dummy.

1126
00:39:45,443 --> 00:39:46,799
- It's her father.

1127
00:39:46,799 --> 00:39:49,882
(music intensifying)

1128
00:39:51,491 --> 00:39:53,663
- Doh, it's Rose Kennedy.

1129
00:39:53,663 --> 00:39:54,746
Looking good.

1130
00:39:58,345 --> 00:40:00,185
- Hey, is that Statler or Waldorf?

1131
00:40:00,185 --> 00:40:01,877
- When you get back to town,

1132
00:40:01,877 --> 00:40:03,807
make out a coroner's report.

1133
00:40:03,807 --> 00:40:06,070
Just put down Jack Flynn as the name.

1134
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:06,971
- Dry's the game.

1135
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:08,639
- Cause of death?

1136
00:40:08,639 --> 00:40:09,639
- It was a spider.

1137
00:40:09,639 --> 00:40:11,261
It drained all the liquid out of his body.

1138
00:40:11,261 --> 00:40:13,537
- Just put down cause unknown,

1139
00:40:13,537 --> 00:40:15,133
and let the coroner worry about the rest.

1140
00:40:15,133 --> 00:40:16,435
- And put some lotion on him or something.

1141
00:40:16,435 --> 00:40:17,677
He looks like hell.

1142
00:40:17,677 --> 00:40:18,897
- That's the trouble with you egg-heads.

1143
00:40:18,897 --> 00:40:20,587
You jump to conclusions.

1144
00:40:20,587 --> 00:40:21,529
I know what I see,

1145
00:40:21,529 --> 00:40:23,163
and I see a dead man,

1146
00:40:23,163 --> 00:40:26,771
but I don't see any spider.
- Do we pretend to know why,

1147
00:40:26,771 --> 00:40:28,741
but I know what I like.

1148
00:40:28,741 --> 00:40:30,857
- Where was the web?

1149
00:40:30,857 --> 00:40:32,690
- Right through there.

1150
00:40:33,755 --> 00:40:35,099
Wait a minute, you don't
know what you're doing.

1151
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:37,353
You can't just walk in there.

1152
00:40:37,353 --> 00:40:38,239
- Why not?

1153
00:40:38,239 --> 00:40:39,505
- You think I'm going
to die a horrible death

1154
00:40:39,505 --> 00:40:41,229
like her old man?

1155
00:40:41,229 --> 00:40:42,137
I'm kidding.

1156
00:40:42,137 --> 00:40:45,117
- Were are you close to him?

1157
00:40:45,117 --> 00:40:46,255
- Nah, nonsense.

1158
00:40:46,255 --> 00:40:49,755
Some circus act from out of town did that.

1159
00:40:51,072 --> 00:40:54,417
- Hmm, yeah, oh, oh,
big, oh, no, ooh, ooh.

1160
00:40:54,417 --> 00:40:56,018
- Find any giant spiders, Sheriff?

1161
00:40:56,018 --> 00:40:57,491
- Ah, shut up.

1162
00:40:57,491 --> 00:40:59,340
- Get that DDT in here quick.

1163
00:40:59,340 --> 00:41:01,527
- PDQ ASAP, you SOB.

1164
00:41:01,527 --> 00:41:04,027
(tense music)

1165
00:41:12,855 --> 00:41:14,211
- Here, you'd better put these on.

1166
00:41:14,211 --> 00:41:15,465
- I suggest you spray that whole cavern

1167
00:41:15,465 --> 00:41:17,750
so it'll get it when it comes back.

1168
00:41:17,750 --> 00:41:20,583
- Hey, who ordered the Hunan beef?

1169
00:41:23,948 --> 00:41:27,031
- They all look like Spy Vs. Spy now.

1170
00:41:31,173 --> 00:41:34,006
- All right, get in the clock now.

1171
00:41:45,353 --> 00:41:46,408
All right, you jump in there.

1172
00:41:46,408 --> 00:41:47,575
You die first.

1173
00:41:53,506 --> 00:41:54,610
- You know, this is great.

1174
00:41:54,610 --> 00:41:56,794
It's really quite comfortable.

1175
00:41:56,794 --> 00:41:58,460
It's nice.

1176
00:41:58,460 --> 00:41:59,293
- Get down here.

1177
00:41:59,293 --> 00:42:02,293
You have got to be kidding me, Pyle.

1178
00:42:04,868 --> 00:42:06,408
- You know, those guys
are pretty much toast,

1179
00:42:06,408 --> 00:42:09,491
or, you know, a light snack at least.

1180
00:42:10,374 --> 00:42:12,624
(mumbling)

1181
00:42:14,115 --> 00:42:16,477
(spraying)

1182
00:42:16,477 --> 00:42:18,411
(screeching)

1183
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:20,661
- Sounds like Jim Morrison.

1184
00:42:23,724 --> 00:42:25,058
(chuckling)

1185
00:42:25,058 --> 00:42:28,141
- I love it when my food's delivered.

1186
00:42:33,834 --> 00:42:36,215
(imitating spider screeching)

1187
00:42:36,215 --> 00:42:37,048
- Uh-oh.

1188
00:42:38,377 --> 00:42:40,606
- Help me, help me!

1189
00:42:40,606 --> 00:42:42,759
- No, Dr. Earhart, no!

1190
00:42:42,759 --> 00:42:44,574
- So that's what happened to him.

1191
00:42:44,574 --> 00:42:46,197
- Wow.

1192
00:42:46,197 --> 00:42:47,030
- Enjoy.

1193
00:42:50,395 --> 00:42:53,338
(screaming)

1194
00:42:53,338 --> 00:42:55,903
- Oh, I'll get a giant
paper towel and smush it.

1195
00:42:55,903 --> 00:42:58,776
- Ugh.
- Not him, the spider.

1196
00:42:58,776 --> 00:43:00,398
- He died as he lived,

1197
00:43:00,398 --> 00:43:02,815
with jelly all over his face.

1198
00:43:07,962 --> 00:43:11,417
- Oh, everybody would have left him.

1199
00:43:11,417 --> 00:43:14,084
(intense music)

1200
00:43:17,753 --> 00:43:19,547
Oh, it's been a big day.

1201
00:43:19,547 --> 00:43:21,130
I'm tired.
- Mm-hmm.

1202
00:43:25,925 --> 00:43:27,591
- Carol?
- Hey, hey, I've got her.

1203
00:43:27,591 --> 00:43:28,424
She's mine.

1204
00:43:28,424 --> 00:43:31,079
- You think it'd be better if
I talked to your mother first?

1205
00:43:31,079 --> 00:43:32,307
- No, thanks.

1206
00:43:32,307 --> 00:43:33,621
I can do it.

1207
00:43:33,621 --> 00:43:36,204
- I'm ready to believe you can.

1208
00:43:37,048 --> 00:43:39,428
- The box with the bracelet.

1209
00:43:39,428 --> 00:43:40,913
- Are you sure you had it?

1210
00:43:40,913 --> 00:43:41,746
- Better go back.

1211
00:43:41,746 --> 00:43:43,559
- It was in this pocket.

1212
00:43:43,559 --> 00:43:45,743
Maybe I dropped it in there.
- You can't go back there now.

1213
00:43:45,743 --> 00:43:46,951
The place is full of gas.

1214
00:43:46,951 --> 00:43:47,784
- That was me.

1215
00:43:47,784 --> 00:43:49,309
I'm sorry.

1216
00:43:49,309 --> 00:43:52,892
- We'll come back some
other time together.

1217
00:43:55,697 --> 00:43:57,841
- Nice shooting, Mr. Carson.

1218
00:43:57,841 --> 00:44:00,025
- Hey, Haskell, when you get back to town,

1219
00:44:00,025 --> 00:44:01,944
tell old Warren to get right out here

1220
00:44:01,944 --> 00:44:03,407
and board this entrance up.

1221
00:44:03,407 --> 00:44:04,490
- Right, sir.

1222
00:44:06,774 --> 00:44:07,607
- Well, if you do,

1223
00:44:07,607 --> 00:44:09,755
I suggest you put a big wide door in it.

1224
00:44:09,755 --> 00:44:10,913
The whole world is going
to want to come here

1225
00:44:10,913 --> 00:44:13,812
and take a look at that thing down there.

1226
00:44:13,812 --> 00:44:15,135
- What's your idea that
- Water slide maybe?

1227
00:44:15,135 --> 00:44:16,756
the town should charge admission?

1228
00:44:16,756 --> 00:44:18,896
- That isn't what I was thinking of.

1229
00:44:18,896 --> 00:44:20,609
You know what we egg-heads
are like, Sheriff.

1230
00:44:20,609 --> 00:44:21,610
We want to know why this,

1231
00:44:21,610 --> 00:44:22,443
how come that,

1232
00:44:22,443 --> 00:44:23,276
what about the other?

1233
00:44:23,276 --> 00:44:24,109
- Can't finish a sentence.

1234
00:44:24,109 --> 00:44:24,942
- It's a matter of scientific interest

1235
00:44:24,942 --> 00:44:26,131
to find out what made that creature.

1236
00:44:26,131 --> 00:44:27,820
- Hey, you got some deputy on your face.

1237
00:44:27,820 --> 00:44:28,653
- It's too late now.

1238
00:44:28,653 --> 00:44:29,486
It'd dead.

1239
00:44:29,486 --> 00:44:30,338
- The spider is,

1240
00:44:30,338 --> 00:44:32,157
but not the principle
that caused it to grow.

1241
00:44:32,157 --> 00:44:34,503
That's still for us to discover.

1242
00:44:34,503 --> 00:44:35,857
- Well why bother?

1243
00:44:35,857 --> 00:44:37,410
- We have to put an end to it.

1244
00:44:37,410 --> 00:44:38,918
Otherwise there may be more giant spiders

1245
00:44:38,918 --> 00:44:40,366
coming into the world.

1246
00:44:40,366 --> 00:44:41,541
- They may even be
hatching from their eggs

1247
00:44:41,541 --> 00:44:43,572
in some remote spot right now.

1248
00:44:43,572 --> 00:44:44,853
Do you realize how easy it would be

1249
00:44:44,853 --> 00:44:47,300
for them to overcome us humans?

1250
00:44:47,300 --> 00:44:48,244
And instead of being the hunters,

1251
00:44:48,244 --> 00:44:49,315
we'd become the hunted.

1252
00:44:49,315 --> 00:44:50,244
- Heavy.

1253
00:44:50,244 --> 00:44:51,077
- They'd be our masters.

1254
00:44:51,077 --> 00:44:52,866
They'd live on us.

1255
00:44:52,866 --> 00:44:54,697
- What would you suggest
the Sheriff's Office

1256
00:44:54,697 --> 00:44:56,905
of River Falls do about it, Mr. Kingman?

1257
00:44:56,905 --> 00:44:57,963
- Close the beaches.

1258
00:44:57,963 --> 00:44:59,527
- Bring that spider up into the daylight.

1259
00:44:59,527 --> 00:45:02,091
- Time to go, guys.
- Have him studied properly.

1260
00:45:02,091 --> 00:45:05,238
- Now, if you want to do it,
go ahead and leave me out.

1261
00:45:05,238 --> 00:45:06,344
It's not my job,

1262
00:45:06,344 --> 00:45:07,782
and I don't want any part of it.

1263
00:45:07,782 --> 00:45:09,115
- Okay, Sheriff.

1264
00:45:11,599 --> 00:45:14,182
(upbeat music)

1265
00:45:17,821 --> 00:45:19,238
- We are Spidoor!

1266
00:45:20,891 --> 00:45:22,308
- This is going to be really cool.

1267
00:45:22,308 --> 00:45:23,952
- On the count of four.

1268
00:45:23,952 --> 00:45:26,850
Let's wail, one, two, three, four!

1269
00:45:26,850 --> 00:45:28,933
- Let's rock this mother!

1270
00:45:29,781 --> 00:45:31,554
- Hold, hold on, Gypsy.

1271
00:45:31,554 --> 00:45:33,921
This isn't some frivolous,
stupid bubblegum music

1272
00:45:33,921 --> 00:45:35,011
we're trying to play.

1273
00:45:35,011 --> 00:45:36,957
This is an ambitious rock opera.

1274
00:45:36,957 --> 00:45:39,408
- Yeah, kind of like what
Kiss would play, you know?

1275
00:45:39,408 --> 00:45:41,969
- Joel, Joel, Joel, I got news for you.

1276
00:45:41,969 --> 00:45:43,247
Kiss were never cool.

1277
00:45:43,247 --> 00:45:46,640
- Well, everybody back at
Ashwaubenon High School

1278
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:47,801
used to love Kiss.

1279
00:45:47,801 --> 00:45:49,298
- Great, you spent your adolescence

1280
00:45:49,298 --> 00:45:50,414
with a bunch of geeky losers,

1281
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:51,748
and now it's our cross to bear?

1282
00:45:51,748 --> 00:45:53,266
- Nobody calls Ashwaubenon Jaguars

1283
00:45:53,266 --> 00:45:54,333
a bunch of geeky losers.

1284
00:45:54,333 --> 00:45:55,166
- Come on, Joel.

1285
00:45:55,166 --> 00:45:57,057
We were thinking our
rock opera would be more

1286
00:45:57,057 --> 00:45:59,128
along the lines of '70s
progressive rock bands,

1287
00:45:59,128 --> 00:46:02,165
like Yes, Gentle Giant, King Crimson,

1288
00:46:02,165 --> 00:46:03,800
Emerson Lake and Palmer.

1289
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:05,870
(sobbing)

1290
00:46:05,870 --> 00:46:06,703
- What's with her?

1291
00:46:06,703 --> 00:46:07,536
- Take it easy.

1292
00:46:07,536 --> 00:46:08,369
That's okay, honey.

1293
00:46:08,369 --> 00:46:12,080
Don't ever mention Emerson
Lake and Palmer around Gypsy.

1294
00:46:12,080 --> 00:46:13,099
Take it easy.

1295
00:46:13,099 --> 00:46:13,932
That's okay.

1296
00:46:13,932 --> 00:46:15,123
Okay, let's wail you guys.

1297
00:46:15,123 --> 00:46:16,045
- Spidoor!

1298
00:46:16,045 --> 00:46:17,462
- We are Spidoor!

1299
00:46:18,876 --> 00:46:20,967
One, two, three, four!

1300
00:46:20,967 --> 00:46:23,325
(screaming)

1301
00:46:23,325 --> 00:46:26,825
Quick, Cambot, give me Rocket Number Nine.

1302
00:46:31,455 --> 00:46:33,930
- What the Hector Alonzo's going on?

1303
00:46:33,930 --> 00:46:35,356
What's all that bracket down there?

1304
00:46:35,356 --> 00:46:36,189
- Well it's just us.

1305
00:46:36,189 --> 00:46:37,885
We're getting ready to
play our rock opera.

1306
00:46:37,885 --> 00:46:40,149
- You don't have a permit
for electronic instruments.

1307
00:46:40,149 --> 00:46:40,982
I'm sorry.

1308
00:46:40,982 --> 00:46:42,382
Nobody said anything about that.

1309
00:46:42,382 --> 00:46:43,854
- Hey, who are you anyway, Pops?

1310
00:46:43,854 --> 00:46:45,832
- I'm from the planet Xephelodian.

1311
00:46:45,832 --> 00:46:47,637
We provide maintenance
and janitorial services

1312
00:46:47,637 --> 00:46:48,578
for the universe.

1313
00:46:48,578 --> 00:46:51,097
I'm the custodian of the Seventh Galaxy.

1314
00:46:51,097 --> 00:46:53,535
- Wow, a custodian from the Seventh Galaxy

1315
00:46:53,535 --> 00:46:55,065
is from the planet Xephelodian.

1316
00:46:55,065 --> 00:46:56,721
He's perfect for our rock opera!

1317
00:46:56,721 --> 00:46:58,710
- You have got to be kidding me.

1318
00:46:58,710 --> 00:46:59,836
A rock opera?

1319
00:46:59,836 --> 00:47:01,137
Is it femme like Kiss,

1320
00:47:01,137 --> 00:47:02,459
or is it boring and pretentious

1321
00:47:02,459 --> 00:47:04,253
like Emerson Lake and Palmer?

1322
00:47:04,253 --> 00:47:06,001
(groaning, sobbing)

1323
00:47:06,001 --> 00:47:06,834
- Oh no, Gypsy.

1324
00:47:06,834 --> 00:47:09,154
Brain salad surgery.

1325
00:47:09,154 --> 00:47:10,258
- Hey, don't blame me.

1326
00:47:10,258 --> 00:47:11,091
I didn't do it.

1327
00:47:11,091 --> 00:47:12,972
- Don't worry, I'll beam
some sawdust over to you.

1328
00:47:12,972 --> 00:47:14,397
Just let me get it out of my locker.

1329
00:47:14,397 --> 00:47:15,489
Check my keys here.

1330
00:47:15,489 --> 00:47:16,652
Oh, I got to go.

1331
00:47:16,652 --> 00:47:18,569
There's a pep rally on Trielphamagore.

1332
00:47:18,569 --> 00:47:19,700
I got to get a good seat.

1333
00:47:19,700 --> 00:47:20,533
Beat it.

1334
00:47:20,533 --> 00:47:21,699
Quiet for God's sake.

1335
00:47:21,699 --> 00:47:22,782
Keep it down.

1336
00:47:22,782 --> 00:47:24,412
- Great, now we've got
to clean up Gypsy's mess.

1337
00:47:24,412 --> 00:47:25,527
Geez, those high school janitors

1338
00:47:25,527 --> 00:47:27,173
are always so weird and creepy.

1339
00:47:27,173 --> 00:47:29,599
- We should chip in and buy
him something for Christmas,

1340
00:47:29,599 --> 00:47:30,472
you know?

1341
00:47:30,472 --> 00:47:32,279
- Yeah, actually that
stuff would go really good

1342
00:47:32,279 --> 00:47:34,862
with our new Spidoor stage set.

1343
00:47:36,131 --> 00:47:36,964
Let's wail!

1344
00:47:36,964 --> 00:47:37,833
Spidoors are go!

1345
00:47:37,833 --> 00:47:39,422
One, two, three, four!

1346
00:47:39,422 --> 00:47:42,675
(alarm blaring, screaming)

1347
00:47:42,675 --> 00:47:45,842
(doors slamming open)

1348
00:47:52,243 --> 00:47:54,956
I'd like to know what that
janitor has to do with anything.

1349
00:47:54,956 --> 00:47:56,003
- We were just about wail.

1350
00:47:56,003 --> 00:47:57,086
- Oh, thanks.

1351
00:47:58,372 --> 00:47:59,361
- Ooh, those things chafe.

1352
00:47:59,361 --> 00:48:00,890
- Usually if nature produces a freak,

1353
00:48:00,890 --> 00:48:02,363
it dies immediately,

1354
00:48:02,363 --> 00:48:04,375
because it can't adapt itself to life.

1355
00:48:04,375 --> 00:48:06,537
- Kind of like Hudson Hawk.

1356
00:48:06,537 --> 00:48:08,469
- It's what we ordinarily
call a bird spider.

1357
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:11,369
- Yeah, this one's called
a big flipping bird spider.

1358
00:48:11,369 --> 00:48:13,616
- Perfect phrases.

1359
00:48:13,616 --> 00:48:15,616
Perfect in every detail.

1360
00:48:16,587 --> 00:48:17,770
- What's the matter with spiders.

1361
00:48:17,770 --> 00:48:19,937
- On the floor, four eyes.

1362
00:48:21,509 --> 00:48:23,152
- Fraser, are you hurt?

1363
00:48:23,152 --> 00:48:24,787
- Come on, Joe, are you
going to take that from him?

1364
00:48:24,787 --> 00:48:26,109
He's just a big dumb spider.

1365
00:48:26,109 --> 00:48:26,983
Come on.

1366
00:48:26,983 --> 00:48:28,731
- I'm sure it's dead.

1367
00:48:28,731 --> 00:48:30,341
- How come it kicked me?

1368
00:48:30,341 --> 00:48:31,997
- It's just a muscular contraction.

1369
00:48:31,997 --> 00:48:33,159
Davanni's reaction it's called.

1370
00:48:33,159 --> 00:48:34,870
It often happens.

1371
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:36,977
- Not to me, it doesn't.

1372
00:48:36,977 --> 00:48:38,633
If it can do that when it's dead,

1373
00:48:38,633 --> 00:48:40,816
I'd sure hate to meet it somewhere alive.

1374
00:48:40,816 --> 00:48:43,649
- You know, you are funny, Friend.

1375
00:48:46,533 --> 00:48:47,716
- I don't think he's funny.

1376
00:48:47,716 --> 00:48:50,363
Daddy's dead and everyone's making jokes.

1377
00:48:50,363 --> 00:48:52,341
- This music's making me retch, Mom.

1378
00:48:52,341 --> 00:48:53,479
Turn it off.

1379
00:48:53,479 --> 00:48:54,696
- Oh, still upset about Dad?

1380
00:48:54,696 --> 00:48:56,020
That gutter snipe would have traded you

1381
00:48:56,020 --> 00:48:58,008
for a case of German beer any old day.

1382
00:48:58,008 --> 00:48:59,584
- I can't help it, Mother.

1383
00:48:59,584 --> 00:49:00,417
- I know.

1384
00:49:02,093 --> 00:49:03,461
I loved him too.

1385
00:49:03,461 --> 00:49:05,932
- Sometimes, like the day he was sober.

1386
00:49:05,932 --> 00:49:07,990
- I keep thinking it was my fault.

1387
00:49:07,990 --> 00:49:08,910
- Well, granted.

1388
00:49:08,910 --> 00:49:10,410
- How could it be?

1389
00:49:11,486 --> 00:49:12,319
- It never would have happened

1390
00:49:12,319 --> 00:49:14,626
if he hadn't gone to get me that present.

1391
00:49:14,626 --> 00:49:15,868
- Good point.

1392
00:49:15,868 --> 00:49:17,319
- I've lost him.

1393
00:49:17,319 --> 00:49:19,640
- You mustn't think of it that way, Carol.

1394
00:49:19,640 --> 00:49:21,846
- Well, that's all broken up.

1395
00:49:21,846 --> 00:49:24,161
- Drop it in that cave.

1396
00:49:24,161 --> 00:49:26,703
I wanted so much to keep it, Mother.

1397
00:49:26,703 --> 00:49:28,610
- Forget about it now, dear.

1398
00:49:28,610 --> 00:49:30,693
You have your homework to
get ready for tomorrow.

1399
00:49:30,693 --> 00:49:32,315
- I don't want you getting bad grades

1400
00:49:32,315 --> 00:49:34,648
just 'cause Dad's worm food.

1401
00:49:35,888 --> 00:49:37,053
- Oh, and I forgot.

1402
00:49:37,053 --> 00:49:39,845
Mike called you twice before
you got home from school,

1403
00:49:39,845 --> 00:49:41,753
and said he would be at
his father's theater.

1404
00:49:41,753 --> 00:49:42,791
- His father!

1405
00:49:42,791 --> 00:49:45,374
(mock sobbing)

1406
00:49:48,120 --> 00:49:50,703
(gentle music)

1407
00:49:54,625 --> 00:49:57,118
- Dial 1-900-Boring-Boyfriend.

1408
00:49:57,118 --> 00:49:59,625
He'd love to talk to you about
his uncle from Milwaukee.

1409
00:49:59,625 --> 00:50:00,625
- Right now.

1410
00:50:02,282 --> 00:50:03,478
- Hello, Mr. Simpson.

1411
00:50:03,478 --> 00:50:05,061
Can I talk to Mike?

1412
00:50:06,468 --> 00:50:09,147
- Hey, what kind of sin must a man commit

1413
00:50:09,147 --> 00:50:10,647
in a single night.

1414
00:50:12,970 --> 00:50:13,862
- Mike?

1415
00:50:13,862 --> 00:50:16,114
You're wanted on the phone.

1416
00:50:16,114 --> 00:50:18,125
- And I get my shirts from the laundry.

1417
00:50:18,125 --> 00:50:19,924
(chuckling)

1418
00:50:19,924 --> 00:50:24,341
- Oh boy, I get to walk past
that poster again, cool.

1419
00:50:30,037 --> 00:50:31,120
- Everywhere.

1420
00:50:33,356 --> 00:50:34,553
- Hi, Mike.

1421
00:50:34,553 --> 00:50:35,720
This is Carol.

1422
00:50:36,601 --> 00:50:39,098
You said you'd take me out to
the cave to find the bracelet.

1423
00:50:39,098 --> 00:50:39,931
- I lied.

1424
00:50:39,931 --> 00:50:41,189
- You don't mean right now, do you?

1425
00:50:41,189 --> 00:50:43,029
- If you can get away.

1426
00:50:43,029 --> 00:50:44,191
Please, Mike?

1427
00:50:44,191 --> 00:50:45,024
- Carol, not today.

1428
00:50:45,024 --> 00:50:46,283
My dad just got in a new picture

1429
00:50:46,283 --> 00:50:48,122
and I haven't even seen it yet.

1430
00:50:48,122 --> 00:50:49,296
Something about puppet people.

1431
00:50:49,296 --> 00:50:50,776
It sounds pretty wild.

1432
00:50:50,776 --> 00:50:51,609
- Please?

1433
00:50:51,609 --> 00:50:53,917
- Shame on you, Bert I. Gordon.

1434
00:50:53,917 --> 00:50:54,750
- Okay, Carol.

1435
00:50:54,750 --> 00:50:56,945
I think I can borrow Joe's car again.

1436
00:50:56,945 --> 00:50:59,819
- Only don't come by the house for me.

1437
00:50:59,819 --> 00:51:02,465
I don't want Mother to
know I'm going out there.

1438
00:51:02,465 --> 00:51:03,298
- All right, I'll be,

1439
00:51:03,298 --> 00:51:05,396
I'll be down at the corner in 15 minutes.

1440
00:51:05,396 --> 00:51:06,896
- I'll be waiting.

1441
00:51:09,203 --> 00:51:10,036
- I'll see ya, Dad.

1442
00:51:10,036 --> 00:51:12,020
I got a date now.

1443
00:51:12,020 --> 00:51:13,387
- Where will you be?

1444
00:51:13,387 --> 00:51:15,207
I said, where would you be if I want you?

1445
00:51:15,207 --> 00:51:16,333
- Wait, aren't you going to watch

1446
00:51:16,333 --> 00:51:19,989
that wonderful Bert I. Gordon movie?

1447
00:51:19,989 --> 00:51:22,822
- It looks like an ad for Dockers.

1448
00:51:25,510 --> 00:51:26,343
- Old high school.

1449
00:51:26,343 --> 00:51:27,217
- Hey, Joe!

1450
00:51:27,217 --> 00:51:29,294
- Hey, where are you going
with that gun in your hand?

1451
00:51:29,294 --> 00:51:30,127
- Hi.

1452
00:51:30,127 --> 00:51:32,846
- Hey, you remember that
five bucks I loaned you?

1453
00:51:32,846 --> 00:51:34,066
- Sure, it was last Christmas

1454
00:51:34,066 --> 00:51:34,916
and I paid it back.

1455
00:51:34,916 --> 00:51:37,022
- All I mean is I'm your friend.

1456
00:51:37,022 --> 00:51:37,855
You know that, don't you?

1457
00:51:37,855 --> 00:51:38,778
- You want to borrow five bucks is all?

1458
00:51:38,778 --> 00:51:39,611
- No, no.

1459
00:51:40,712 --> 00:51:43,150
Could Carol and I use your
wagon for a couple of hours?

1460
00:51:43,150 --> 00:51:43,983
- Again?

1461
00:51:45,092 --> 00:51:46,563
What's the big deal?

1462
00:51:46,563 --> 00:51:48,682
- What do I have sucker stamped my head?

1463
00:51:48,682 --> 00:51:49,614
- Look, we're friends, Joe.

1464
00:51:49,614 --> 00:51:50,447
Just remember that.

1465
00:51:50,447 --> 00:51:51,304
- Why don't you come to the rehearsal?

1466
00:51:51,304 --> 00:51:52,442
- Look, my mouth is getting tired.

1467
00:51:52,442 --> 00:51:53,512
Are we friends or aren't we?

1468
00:51:53,512 --> 00:51:54,524
- Okay, okay.

1469
00:51:54,524 --> 00:51:55,443
The car's in the driveway.

1470
00:51:55,443 --> 00:51:56,306
You'll find the keys in-

1471
00:51:56,306 --> 00:51:57,170
- The glove compartment.

1472
00:51:57,170 --> 00:51:58,031
Where else?

1473
00:51:58,031 --> 00:51:59,526
- Why do I have so many friends?

1474
00:51:59,526 --> 00:52:00,412
- Thanks, Joe.

1475
00:52:00,412 --> 00:52:01,688
- Hey, that's Harvey Keitel.

1476
00:52:01,688 --> 00:52:02,598
- Oh, the pain.

1477
00:52:02,598 --> 00:52:03,431
- Come on, Joe.

1478
00:52:03,431 --> 00:52:04,919
We've got problems.

1479
00:52:04,919 --> 00:52:06,146
No show today, it's off limits.

1480
00:52:06,146 --> 00:52:08,313
- Maybe it's a frat party?

1481
00:52:12,688 --> 00:52:13,880
- But we've got to get in.

1482
00:52:13,880 --> 00:52:15,596
The dance is tomorrow night.

1483
00:52:15,596 --> 00:52:17,791
Other cats will have a blast
if we don't swing solid.

1484
00:52:17,791 --> 00:52:19,541
- Yeah, what he said.

1485
00:52:20,944 --> 00:52:22,082
- Hey, let's get the janitor.

1486
00:52:22,082 --> 00:52:22,915
- Janitor.

1487
00:52:22,915 --> 00:52:23,748
- Janitor.

1488
00:52:23,748 --> 00:52:25,829
- That's how it fits in.

1489
00:52:25,829 --> 00:52:29,074
- They can't hang us for trying, can they?

1490
00:52:29,074 --> 00:52:30,705
Hugo?

1491
00:52:30,705 --> 00:52:31,538
Hey, Hugo!

1492
00:52:31,538 --> 00:52:32,371
- Hugo!

1493
00:52:32,371 --> 00:52:33,204
- Looking for his car?

1494
00:52:33,204 --> 00:52:35,068
- Who's calling Hugo?

1495
00:52:35,068 --> 00:52:35,901
- There he is.

1496
00:52:35,901 --> 00:52:36,919
- Well now, what's the matter here?

1497
00:52:36,919 --> 00:52:37,752
- Someone threw up.

1498
00:52:37,752 --> 00:52:39,092
Got some sawdust?
- We want in.

1499
00:52:39,092 --> 00:52:40,978
- We've got to develop our talents.

1500
00:52:40,978 --> 00:52:43,452
- You'll have to use the
auditorium til further notice.

1501
00:52:43,452 --> 00:52:44,786
Principal's orders.

1502
00:52:44,786 --> 00:52:45,878
- No can do.

1503
00:52:45,878 --> 00:52:47,257
The drama class is there.

1504
00:52:47,257 --> 00:52:48,290
- I can't help that.

1505
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:49,270
Thing here is tricking up.

1506
00:52:49,270 --> 00:52:52,156
Told me particular not to let nobody in.

1507
00:52:52,156 --> 00:52:52,989
- Particular.

1508
00:52:52,989 --> 00:52:53,927
- Well, he didn't mean us.

1509
00:52:53,927 --> 00:52:55,228
He met squares.

1510
00:52:55,228 --> 00:52:57,228
We're the coolest zoologists in town.

1511
00:52:57,228 --> 00:52:58,423
- No sirree.

1512
00:52:58,423 --> 00:53:00,610
The moving people are coming here tonight

1513
00:53:00,610 --> 00:53:02,333
to move that thing to the university.

1514
00:53:02,333 --> 00:53:03,542
- Help me find my chin.

1515
00:53:03,542 --> 00:53:05,034
- Want to do afterwards.

1516
00:53:05,034 --> 00:53:06,427
- In the dead of night?

1517
00:53:06,427 --> 00:53:08,711
Hugo, we're only little kids.
- What are you talking about?

1518
00:53:08,711 --> 00:53:09,682
You're 42.

1519
00:53:09,682 --> 00:53:11,182
- Well, all right.

1520
00:53:12,178 --> 00:53:13,258
Your mom's first.

1521
00:53:13,258 --> 00:53:14,091
- Rubbish.

1522
00:53:14,091 --> 00:53:16,986
- Now I want you to behave yourself.

1523
00:53:16,986 --> 00:53:19,458
Don't monkey with that thing.

1524
00:53:19,458 --> 00:53:20,550
- Dig that?

1525
00:53:20,550 --> 00:53:22,310
Now the first guy who
steps on daddy long legs

1526
00:53:22,310 --> 00:53:23,966
is going to hear from Hugo!

1527
00:53:23,966 --> 00:53:24,799
- Yeah.

1528
00:53:24,799 --> 00:53:29,256
- Yeah, I got to go play
with my pig, Arnold.

1529
00:53:29,256 --> 00:53:30,970
(tense music)

1530
00:53:30,970 --> 00:53:31,803
- Say.

1531
00:53:39,478 --> 00:53:41,848
- Imagine if they had the
budget to show it all.

1532
00:53:41,848 --> 00:53:43,571
(whistling)

1533
00:53:43,571 --> 00:53:48,276
- Look, spider, all of us got
together and voted you out.

1534
00:53:48,276 --> 00:53:50,471
- It's big, all right.

1535
00:53:50,471 --> 00:53:52,278
- Hey, maybe the drama class
is through with the auditorium.

1536
00:53:52,278 --> 00:53:53,118
Let's blow this place.

1537
00:53:53,118 --> 00:53:54,440
It gives me the creeps.

1538
00:53:54,440 --> 00:53:55,531
- What is it, Superman?

1539
00:53:55,531 --> 00:53:56,430
Chickening out?

1540
00:53:56,430 --> 00:53:57,681
- Well, certainly not.

1541
00:53:57,681 --> 00:54:01,113
- Well then, stop goofing off, huh?

1542
00:54:01,113 --> 00:54:03,530
- That's a nice process shot.

1543
00:54:10,113 --> 00:54:13,576
(playing piano)

1544
00:54:13,576 --> 00:54:14,980
Okay, we'll open with Rite of Spring

1545
00:54:14,980 --> 00:54:16,498
and then kick into Blue Suede Shoes.

1546
00:54:16,498 --> 00:54:18,084
- All right, let's start
with the opening number.

1547
00:54:18,084 --> 00:54:19,635
And don't go to sleep on it.

1548
00:54:19,635 --> 00:54:20,923
Play with everything you've got.

1549
00:54:20,923 --> 00:54:23,577
- Especially the instruments.

1550
00:54:23,577 --> 00:54:24,410
- Sorry.

1551
00:54:26,192 --> 00:54:27,839
- Play good and loud.

1552
00:54:27,839 --> 00:54:29,481
- More rock bands could use conductors.

1553
00:54:29,481 --> 00:54:30,314
- Okay!

1554
00:54:30,314 --> 00:54:33,037
(screaming)

1555
00:54:33,037 --> 00:54:35,659
- It's the New Christy Minstrels.

1556
00:54:35,659 --> 00:54:37,002
- Hey, what goes on here?

1557
00:54:37,002 --> 00:54:39,016
- It's the drama class, what else?

1558
00:54:39,016 --> 00:54:41,062
- All right, either come in or get out.

1559
00:54:41,062 --> 00:54:42,614
Don't stand there and scream.

1560
00:54:42,614 --> 00:54:43,447
We're rehearsing.

1561
00:54:43,447 --> 00:54:45,558
- Theater freaks.

1562
00:54:45,558 --> 00:54:47,271
- One, two, three, four.

1563
00:54:47,271 --> 00:54:48,104
- Four and a half.

1564
00:54:48,104 --> 00:54:50,412
(rock and roll music)

1565
00:54:50,412 --> 00:54:51,713
- Missed the downbeat.

1566
00:54:51,713 --> 00:54:53,630
- Well, okay, let's go.

1567
00:54:55,350 --> 00:54:56,633
(yelling in surprise)

1568
00:54:56,633 --> 00:54:58,751
- Oh, they walked right through us.

1569
00:54:58,751 --> 00:54:59,834
That's weird.

1570
00:55:07,052 --> 00:55:09,613
- Now he's doing his Charlie Callas.

1571
00:55:09,613 --> 00:55:12,863
I think this guy peaked in high school.

1572
00:55:15,436 --> 00:55:16,936
- Come on, boogie.

1573
00:55:18,071 --> 00:55:19,346
Everybody, come on.

1574
00:55:19,346 --> 00:55:20,806
- Oh, now they're Voguing.

1575
00:55:20,806 --> 00:55:22,901
- Yep, strike a pose.

1576
00:55:22,901 --> 00:55:23,992
- Geez, I hate this music.

1577
00:55:23,992 --> 00:55:25,661
Don't you know any "Spider" John Koerner?

1578
00:55:25,661 --> 00:55:26,494
Come on.

1579
00:55:27,614 --> 00:55:29,447
- Hey, swing it, cats.

1580
00:55:30,570 --> 00:55:34,079
Ooh, you know, you should
really get that guy on a stool.

1581
00:55:34,079 --> 00:55:34,986
- Hike up your pants now.

