and affordable toys

2103
01:15:00,989 --> 01:15:03,588
that are safe, soft, and colorful.

2104
01:15:03,588 --> 01:15:04,421
Goodnight.

2105
01:15:04,421 --> 01:15:05,969
- And may God bless.

2106
01:15:05,969 --> 01:15:08,552
(upbeat music)

2107
01:15:12,534 --> 01:15:13,617
- Mike, look!

2108
01:15:13,617 --> 01:15:15,273
- Oh, we're coming out
of the game thing then.

2109
01:15:15,273 --> 01:15:16,106
- That was neat.

2110
01:15:16,106 --> 01:15:17,986
- Certainly was a neat game thing we did.

2111
01:15:17,986 --> 01:15:19,560
Oh boy.

2112
01:15:19,560 --> 01:15:21,308
- I tell you there have
been people through here.

2113
01:15:21,308 --> 01:15:23,056
- Jack Weston!

2114
01:15:23,056 --> 01:15:24,160
Or George.

2115
01:15:24,160 --> 01:15:26,819
- George Weston, lost?

2116
01:15:26,819 --> 01:15:27,652
- Hello?

2117
01:15:27,652 --> 01:15:28,485
I'm George Weston.

2118
01:15:28,485 --> 01:15:29,552
- 1902.

2119
01:15:29,552 --> 01:15:30,385
- Mike!

2120
01:15:30,385 --> 01:15:31,468
- Ugh, grody.

2121
01:15:33,903 --> 01:15:37,099
- He must have starved to death.

2122
01:15:37,099 --> 01:15:40,009
I'm getting awfully worried, Mike.

2123
01:15:40,009 --> 01:15:41,987
- Me too, Carol.

2124
01:15:41,987 --> 01:15:43,709
- Why did I ever have
to bring you down here?

2125
01:15:43,709 --> 01:15:44,584
Go, Mike.

2126
01:15:44,584 --> 01:15:46,691
- All you do is bring me down, babe.

2127
01:15:46,691 --> 01:15:48,887
- Don't let her bring you down.
It's only castles burning.

2128
01:15:48,887 --> 01:15:50,853
- What do you suppose
your mother's thinking?

2129
01:15:50,853 --> 01:15:51,898
- Well, they wouldn't tell her.

2130
01:15:51,898 --> 01:15:54,051
She's in the hospital having a baby.

2131
01:15:54,051 --> 01:15:55,017
- And what about your dad?

2132
01:15:55,017 --> 01:15:57,234
- Dad? We're still trying
to find out who he is.

2133
01:15:57,234 --> 01:16:00,051
- I think he can take it.

2134
01:16:00,051 --> 01:16:01,551
- My mother can't.

2135
01:16:03,365 --> 01:16:05,137
Not after what happened to my father.

2136
01:16:05,137 --> 01:16:07,358
- Don't make yourself feel bad, Carol.

2137
01:16:07,358 --> 01:16:09,358
- I can do that for you.

2138
01:16:12,672 --> 01:16:15,339
- Don't you worry about it then.

2139
01:16:17,133 --> 01:16:19,698
- All of a sudden I feel hungry.

2140
01:16:19,698 --> 01:16:21,308
- Me too.
- Not for spider.

2141
01:16:21,308 --> 01:16:23,168
- I just remembered I've
got a candy bar with me.

2142
01:16:23,168 --> 01:16:25,585
- What are you going to have?

2143
01:16:28,312 --> 01:16:29,895
- It's a Clark Bar.

2144
01:16:30,750 --> 01:16:32,842
- Ugh, must have gotten
warm in your pocket.

2145
01:16:32,842 --> 01:16:37,604
It is good food, however.
(eerie screeching)

2146
01:16:37,604 --> 01:16:40,854
- Hey, did you just make a yummy noise?

2147
01:16:45,249 --> 01:16:46,872
- No, this always happens at dinner.

2148
01:16:46,872 --> 01:16:50,705
Have your little friend
go home now, will you?

2149
01:16:51,574 --> 01:16:54,334
- Convoy with Kris
Kristofferson and Ali MacGraw.

2150
01:16:54,334 --> 01:16:57,061
Up next is Kenny Rogers in Six Pack.

2151
01:16:57,061 --> 01:16:58,083
- Good movie.

2152
01:16:58,083 --> 01:17:00,994
♪ We are the men of Texico ♪

2153
01:17:00,994 --> 01:17:03,244
♪ The star ♪

2154
01:17:07,858 --> 01:17:09,240
- All right, you men, make it snappy.

2155
01:17:09,240 --> 01:17:11,230
Let's get that gear off that truck.

2156
01:17:11,230 --> 01:17:14,370
- Break out the little cocktail weenies.

2157
01:17:14,370 --> 01:17:15,404
- I'll just stay out here

2158
01:17:15,404 --> 01:17:18,904
and bark out belligerent fat-assed orders.

2159
01:17:20,038 --> 01:17:21,694
- Good, good, keep it coming.

2160
01:17:21,694 --> 01:17:23,111
Come on, come on.

2161
01:17:25,582 --> 01:17:27,316
Come on, oh, come on, Pops.

2162
01:17:27,316 --> 01:17:28,446
Is that all you can carry?

2163
01:17:28,446 --> 01:17:30,516
Take two next time.

2164
01:17:30,516 --> 01:17:31,446
- Yeah, case of Shabbos.

2165
01:17:31,446 --> 01:17:32,724
Good boy, good boy.

2166
01:17:32,724 --> 01:17:35,597
- Carol always lets me know
when she isn't coming home.

2167
01:17:35,597 --> 01:17:37,529
Always, but today.

2168
01:17:37,529 --> 01:17:38,362
I don't know.

2169
01:17:38,362 --> 01:17:40,137
She just wasn't herself.

2170
01:17:40,137 --> 01:17:43,206
She attached too much
importance to that bracelet.

2171
01:17:43,206 --> 01:17:45,867
Oh, I hope she and Mike haven't
gone back into that cave.

2172
01:17:45,867 --> 01:17:47,450
- Shut up, shut up!

2173
01:17:50,479 --> 01:17:51,312
- Carol, do you see?

2174
01:17:51,312 --> 01:17:53,156
This is the place where we got lost.

2175
01:17:53,156 --> 01:17:54,776
Oh, I know the way is through there.

2176
01:17:54,776 --> 01:17:56,389
- But the spider, Mike.

2177
01:17:56,389 --> 01:17:57,309
- We stay here, it will find us.

2178
01:17:57,309 --> 01:17:58,345
Come on, let's run for it.

2179
01:17:58,345 --> 01:17:59,655
- Let's find this place where we're safe

2180
01:17:59,655 --> 01:18:01,905
from these processed shots.

2181
01:18:05,082 --> 01:18:05,923
- There's the hole we fell through.

2182
01:18:05,923 --> 01:18:07,567
We haven't got far to go now.

2183
01:18:07,567 --> 01:18:09,992
I'll climb through the web.

2184
01:18:09,992 --> 01:18:13,487
- Hey, I saw this in Beastmaster
about 60 times on cable.

2185
01:18:13,487 --> 01:18:14,789
- Right after Roadhouse.

2186
01:18:14,789 --> 01:18:15,956
- Good movies.

2187
01:18:20,517 --> 01:18:21,350
- I'm stuck!

2188
01:18:21,350 --> 01:18:22,219
- Give me your hand.

2189
01:18:22,219 --> 01:18:23,052
Give me your hand.

2190
01:18:23,052 --> 01:18:24,885
- Hey, Moe, I'm stuck.

2191
01:18:26,681 --> 01:18:28,705
(eerie screeching)

2192
01:18:28,705 --> 01:18:29,693
- It's coming!

2193
01:18:29,693 --> 01:18:31,499
- It sounds like my
grandma in the morning.

2194
01:18:31,499 --> 01:18:32,845
- Let's get that extra
dynamite out of here.

2195
01:18:32,845 --> 01:18:33,678
- Ex-try?

2196
01:18:37,237 --> 01:18:38,963
- Well, that'll be the
end of our spider's night,

2197
01:18:38,963 --> 01:18:40,202
eh Kingman?

2198
01:18:40,202 --> 01:18:41,133
(chuckling)

2199
01:18:41,133 --> 01:18:43,170
- Maybe, but you said last time.

2200
01:18:43,170 --> 01:18:44,723
- Now this time it's for sure.

2201
01:18:44,723 --> 01:18:45,771
It's got to die.

2202
01:18:45,771 --> 01:18:47,231
No living organism can survive for long

2203
01:18:47,231 --> 01:18:49,415
once its food supply is cut off.

2204
01:18:49,415 --> 01:18:51,485
- We'll be ready to blow her
up in a couple of seconds.

2205
01:18:51,485 --> 01:18:52,969
- Let her blow when you're ready.

2206
01:18:52,969 --> 01:18:56,879
- Well, surely they'll see
our car at the entrance.

2207
01:18:56,879 --> 01:18:58,087
- I don't think so.

2208
01:18:58,087 --> 01:18:59,431
- Get back, all you men.

2209
01:18:59,431 --> 01:19:00,536
I don't want anyone hurt.

2210
01:19:00,536 --> 01:19:02,502
- Except for the kids in the cave.

2211
01:19:02,502 --> 01:19:04,052
(chuckling)

2212
01:19:04,052 --> 01:19:05,052
I can't see.

2213
01:19:08,839 --> 01:19:11,485
- Can't you carry more than a hammer?

2214
01:19:11,485 --> 01:19:14,061
(tense music)

2215
01:19:14,061 --> 01:19:15,291
- Then when Carol was three-

2216
01:19:15,291 --> 01:19:18,373
- Shut up, would you shut up?

2217
01:19:18,373 --> 01:19:20,213
- Isn't that Joe's car over there?

2218
01:19:20,213 --> 01:19:21,397
- Yes, it is.

2219
01:19:21,397 --> 01:19:22,314
- Why, yes.

2220
01:19:27,251 --> 01:19:28,585
- It's my car now!

2221
01:19:28,585 --> 01:19:30,214
(cackling)

2222
01:19:30,214 --> 01:19:31,863
(screaming)

2223
01:19:31,863 --> 01:19:34,946
(explosion rumbling)

2224
01:19:37,007 --> 01:19:40,845
- Oops, sorry kids.
- It's a trampoline.

2225
01:19:40,845 --> 01:19:43,215
- You know, just dawns on me.

2226
01:19:43,215 --> 01:19:44,492
I wonder if anyone is in that cave?

2227
01:19:44,492 --> 01:19:45,481
Maybe we should have checked.

2228
01:19:45,481 --> 01:19:46,493
- You sealed them up.

2229
01:19:46,493 --> 01:19:48,873
You're going to have to open
that cave and get them out.

2230
01:19:48,873 --> 01:19:49,968
- Now don't get excited.

2231
01:19:49,968 --> 01:19:52,314
We're going to do
everything for them we can.

2232
01:19:52,314 --> 01:19:54,142
How do we go about it, Haskell?

2233
01:19:54,142 --> 01:19:55,614
- Open up the cave again?

2234
01:19:55,614 --> 01:19:57,280
- Hmm.
- That's easy to say, Sheriff,

2235
01:19:57,280 --> 01:19:59,248
but it's going to take some doing.

2236
01:19:59,248 --> 01:20:01,870
Well we blew up tons of earth
and rock over that opening.

2237
01:20:01,870 --> 01:20:03,822
Brought half a hillside down.

2238
01:20:03,822 --> 01:20:05,830
- This guy must be Bert
Gordon's nephew or something.

2239
01:20:05,830 --> 01:20:06,889
- We better start clearing it away.

2240
01:20:06,889 --> 01:20:08,127
- It'll take days or maybe a week.

2241
01:20:08,127 --> 01:20:09,254
- There isn't that much time.

2242
01:20:09,254 --> 01:20:10,199
If the spider doesn't get them,

2243
01:20:10,199 --> 01:20:11,934
the bad air will.

2244
01:20:11,934 --> 01:20:13,051
- Well then we better get going,

2245
01:20:13,051 --> 01:20:14,706
the sooner, the better.

2246
01:20:14,706 --> 01:20:15,786
You've got a car.

2247
01:20:15,786 --> 01:20:17,798
Go into town and get them
to send out a bulldozer.

2248
01:20:17,798 --> 01:20:20,076
- And some sandwiches, whoever you are.

2249
01:20:20,076 --> 01:20:20,963
- See that flat shelf,

2250
01:20:20,963 --> 01:20:22,318
a little higher up the mountain?

2251
01:20:22,318 --> 01:20:26,170
Suppose we dug straight down from there?

2252
01:20:26,170 --> 01:20:27,844
- How about it, Haskell?

2253
01:20:27,844 --> 01:20:29,276
- Looks good to me.

2254
01:20:29,276 --> 01:20:31,773
Let's get those ropes, picks,
and shovels out of that truck.

2255
01:20:31,773 --> 01:20:33,714
Here's where we going to work.

2256
01:20:33,714 --> 01:20:34,547
- Who is that guy?

2257
01:20:34,547 --> 01:20:36,880
He's stinks like mummy meat.

2258
01:20:38,694 --> 01:20:40,421
- First they want us to close the cave,

2259
01:20:40,421 --> 01:20:43,718
then they want us to open the cave.

2260
01:20:43,718 --> 01:20:45,824
- What's your problem?

2261
01:20:45,824 --> 01:20:48,526
- You don't want to look at
it like that, Mrs. Flynn.

2262
01:20:48,526 --> 01:20:51,022
You've got to remember
that cave is a big place

2263
01:20:51,022 --> 01:20:52,841
and those kids have a lot of sense.

2264
01:20:52,841 --> 01:20:55,380
They'll find places where
the spider can't get at them.

2265
01:20:55,380 --> 01:20:56,760
- If we can dig our way in,

2266
01:20:56,760 --> 01:20:58,508
what's to keep it from getting at us?

2267
01:20:58,508 --> 01:20:59,421
- I don't know.

2268
01:20:59,421 --> 01:21:01,261
What do you say, Kingman?

2269
01:21:01,261 --> 01:21:03,238
- We got to have some kind
of an effective weapon.

2270
01:21:03,238 --> 01:21:05,999
I guess that that's obvious.

2271
01:21:05,999 --> 01:21:07,860
That power line across the hills.

2272
01:21:07,860 --> 01:21:08,693
- Which one?

2273
01:21:08,693 --> 01:21:09,526
Oh, that one?

2274
01:21:09,526 --> 01:21:10,359
- We could bring a cable over from there.

2275
01:21:10,359 --> 01:21:11,276
- What for?

2276
01:21:12,896 --> 01:21:14,472
- Get better reception.
- Electrocute the beast.

2277
01:21:14,472 --> 01:21:16,972
(tense music)

2278
01:21:18,636 --> 01:21:20,397
- Big, sweaty men working long hours

2279
01:21:20,397 --> 01:21:21,613
to get the job done,

2280
01:21:21,613 --> 01:21:23,328
desperately in need of Aqua Velva.

2281
01:21:23,328 --> 01:21:25,017
- Quarter mile of insulated copper cable

2282
01:21:25,017 --> 01:21:26,582
this side of Springdale.

2283
01:21:26,582 --> 01:21:27,527
- Check in my trunk.

2284
01:21:27,527 --> 01:21:31,584
- Seems to me I saw a lot
of that stuff in there.

2285
01:21:31,584 --> 01:21:33,218
- Do you want to go for
it in the truck, Simpson?

2286
01:21:33,218 --> 01:21:34,402
- Yeah.
- Kinky.

2287
01:21:34,402 --> 01:21:37,069
- Go for it in the truck.
- What?

2288
01:21:38,525 --> 01:21:39,729
- How's it coming?

2289
01:21:39,729 --> 01:21:42,729
- Not bad, but we have plenty to go.

2290
01:21:43,719 --> 01:21:45,925
- Stay off the moon.

2291
01:21:45,925 --> 01:21:48,030
(imitating wind whistling)

2292
01:21:48,030 --> 01:21:49,697
- Oh, hey, what the?

2293
01:21:54,194 --> 01:21:58,141
- Hey, did the earth move for you, honey?

2294
01:21:58,141 --> 01:21:59,391
That was great.

2295
01:22:04,084 --> 01:22:05,869
- Feeling a little rocky this morning.

2296
01:22:05,869 --> 01:22:08,619
- I really got stoned last night.

2297
01:22:10,445 --> 01:22:11,278
- Carol!

2298
01:22:13,987 --> 01:22:14,820
Carol!

2299
01:22:17,725 --> 01:22:19,025
Carol!

2300
01:22:19,025 --> 01:22:20,858
- Oh, I feel so dirty.

2301
01:22:22,037 --> 01:22:23,325
- Where is it?

2302
01:22:23,325 --> 01:22:26,361
- Looks like the Wall
concert got out of hand.

2303
01:22:26,361 --> 01:22:27,194
- Let's go.

2304
01:22:27,194 --> 01:22:28,027
Can you make it?

2305
01:22:28,027 --> 01:22:29,694
- I'll be all right.

2306
01:22:31,157 --> 01:22:32,733
- Wait, you got your bracelet?

2307
01:22:32,733 --> 01:22:34,757
- Would you forget that darn bracelet.

2308
01:22:34,757 --> 01:22:36,137
- But I need my bracelet.

2309
01:22:36,137 --> 01:22:37,637
- Oh, fine.
- Wait!

2310
01:22:39,044 --> 01:22:41,627
(upbeat music)

2311
01:22:47,085 --> 01:22:49,293
- Yeah, I got this
dynamite from the coyote.

2312
01:22:49,293 --> 01:22:52,210
Hope it doesn't roll back up on me.

2313
01:22:56,595 --> 01:22:58,928
(whistling)

2314
01:23:02,057 --> 01:23:04,666
- Now watch the old walrus move now.

2315
01:23:04,666 --> 01:23:06,916
(laughing)

2316
01:23:08,519 --> 01:23:09,588
- Is this the place we came in?

2317
01:23:09,588 --> 01:23:10,740
- I'm sure it was!

2318
01:23:10,740 --> 01:23:11,821
- Not anymore.

2319
01:23:11,821 --> 01:23:13,166
- They blew up the opening.

2320
01:23:13,166 --> 01:23:14,914
- What do we do?

2321
01:23:14,914 --> 01:23:16,478
- Panic?

2322
01:23:16,478 --> 01:23:18,355
(rumbling)

2323
01:23:18,355 --> 01:23:19,458
- What was that?

2324
01:23:19,458 --> 01:23:21,253
- Oh, some blasted thing.

2325
01:23:21,253 --> 01:23:24,085
- It sounds like blasting. I
bet they know we're in here.

2326
01:23:24,085 --> 01:23:25,669
I bet they're trying to get us out!

2327
01:23:25,669 --> 01:23:26,761
Help!

2328
01:23:26,761 --> 01:23:27,932
- [Both] Help!

2329
01:23:27,932 --> 01:23:28,843
- Help!

2330
01:23:28,843 --> 01:23:29,676
- Help!

2331
01:23:29,676 --> 01:23:30,509
- Help!

2332
01:23:31,532 --> 01:23:32,365
- They can't hear us.

2333
01:23:32,365 --> 01:23:34,995
Maybe if we get closer
to where they're working.

2334
01:23:34,995 --> 01:23:35,835
- Smart.

2335
01:23:35,835 --> 01:23:37,512
- Gee, we got one deer leg.

2336
01:23:37,512 --> 01:23:38,880
We're going to use it everywhere.

2337
01:23:38,880 --> 01:23:41,180
- [Both] Help! Help!

2338
01:23:41,180 --> 01:23:42,815
- [Mike] We're down here!

2339
01:23:42,815 --> 01:23:44,747
- You have to be heard,
understood, and pleasing.

2340
01:23:44,747 --> 01:23:47,747
Use plenty of lip and tongue action.

2341
01:23:49,439 --> 01:23:50,272
- Help.

2342
01:23:51,116 --> 01:23:51,949
- Louder.

2343
01:23:51,949 --> 01:23:53,591
- Help, we're down here.

2344
01:23:53,591 --> 01:23:55,785
(calling for help in distance)

2345
01:23:55,785 --> 01:23:57,488
- Chad, I hear someone.

2346
01:23:57,488 --> 01:23:59,156
- Calvin Klein Jeans.

2347
01:23:59,156 --> 01:24:02,076
- Mike, Carol, we hear you!

2348
01:24:02,076 --> 01:24:03,732
- But we don't care!

2349
01:24:03,732 --> 01:24:04,565
- It's Kingman.

2350
01:24:04,565 --> 01:24:05,572
They heard us!

2351
01:24:05,572 --> 01:24:08,286
(screeching)
- I hear you too.

2352
01:24:08,286 --> 01:24:11,306
(screaming, chuckling)
- If it's not one thing,

2353
01:24:11,306 --> 01:24:12,878
it's another in this crazy cave.

2354
01:24:12,878 --> 01:24:13,711
Whew.

2355
01:24:15,878 --> 01:24:17,028
- Oh look, I got a walleye,

2356
01:24:17,028 --> 01:24:18,099
a couple of northerns.

2357
01:24:18,099 --> 01:24:19,766
No big lunkers here.

2358
01:24:20,984 --> 01:24:23,079
- And this is the power
line foreman, Kingman.

2359
01:24:23,079 --> 01:24:24,539
He's going to help us
when the cable gets here.

2360
01:24:24,539 --> 01:24:25,824
